Task 1.2--------contact and Account Management workflow

1}In Zoho, an Account represents a company, and a Contact is an individual.1. Create Contact Under Existing AccountMethod A (Direct): Go to the Accounts module, click on a specific account, and click "+ New Contact" in the related list. This automatically links the new contact to that account.Method B (Lookup): In the Contacts module, click "+ New Contact". In the "Account Name" field, search for and select an existing account.2. Create Contact Under New AccountIn the Contacts module, click "+ New Contact".In the "Account Name" field, type the name of the new company.Click "+ New [Account Name]" within the dropdown list to create the account on the fly.
validations:1Unique Email: Zoho can validate if a contact's email already exists in the system.Mandatory Fields: "Last Name" is mandatory by default.Validation Rules: Admins can create rules to prevent saving if certain criteria are not met (e.g., checking if a phone number format is correct).Account Association: If a contact is created without an account, it is an "orphan" contact. You can update the "Account Name" field later, but only one at a time.

 In HubSpot, the equivalent structure is "Company" (Parent) and "Contact" (Child).1. Create Contact Under Existing CompanyMethod A (From Company): Navigate to the specific Company record and click "+ Create contact" in the contacts card.Method B (From Contact): Go to Contacts > Create Contact. In the "Company" field, search for and select the existing company.2. Create Contact Under New CompanyGo to Contacts > Create Contact.In the "Company" field, type the new company name.Select the option to create a new company record, which will be automatically associated.

 2)Zoho crm silently allows creation of duplicate email address where as in hubspot crm ,this is strickly blocked by creation a second contact with same email address.
 3)When an account is deleted in Zoho or HubSpot, associated contacts, deals, and activities are typically detached or deleted, depending on the system. When merged, HubSpot consolidates data into a primary record, while Zoho re-parents records.
 4)–1) Zoho CRM typically handles primary contacts by allowing multiple contacts to be associated with an account and designating one as the main contact, while HubSpot CRM uses a highly flexible, relationship-based model focusing on a "Company" record with associated contact records, where any contact can be assigned a "primary" role via property mapping or custom, flexible associations.
 2)Zoho is better for companies that need strict, pre-defined hierarchies and formal "primary" designation.HubSpot is better for teams seeking flexibility, allowing users to define relationships more freely, with a stronger focus on the overall contact-company relationship timeline 



