1)issue:Can a deal exist without an owner? What does that do to pipeline reports? 
>1.Steps to Reproduce (Attempt to "Unassign" a Deal)While you cannot leave the owner field empty, you can simulate unassigned deals by creating a "Dummy/System" user or by transferring ownership to an inactive user.
1.Create a Dummy User (Optional): Go to Setup > Users and Control > Users > +New User and create a user named "Unassigned Pool."Navigate to Deals:
2.Go to the Deals module.Create/Edit a Deal:
3.Click +New Deal or open an existing deal.Change Owner: Locate the Deal Owner field.Reassign: Attempt to change the owner. Note: Zoho requires a user to be selected.
4.Change the owner to the "Unassigned Pool" user created in Step 1.Save: Click Save.
>Actual BehaviourThe Deal is successfully saved, but it is owned by the "Unassigned Pool" user.It does not appear in individual sales reps' "My Deals" view.It appears in the "All Deals" view or reports filtered by the "Unassigned Pool" owner.
>Expected BehaviourIn a properly managed CRM, every deal should be owned by a functional, active user to ensure it is worked on.If a deal is created via API without an owner mapping, Zoho will typically assign it to the user whose API token was used.

2)issue Can you close a deal as Won if required fields are empty?
Steps to Reproduce:
1. Go to Setup > Customization > Modules and Fields > Deals.
2. Make a field (e.g.,"Amount") mandatory.
3. Create a deal, fill in the field, and save. 
4.Edit the deal, remove the data from that field, and change the Stage to "Closed Won".Save.
> Actual Behaviour: The deal saves with empty required fields if the validation rule is not properly applied to the closing action.
> Expected Behaviour: A pop-up should alert the user that the field is mandatory to move to "Closed Won".

3) issue – Does re-opening a Closed Lost deal reset its original close date in reports?
>Steps to Reproduce: 
1) Navigate to the Deals module. 
2) Open a deal that is currently in a Closed Lost stage.
3) Note the Closing Date (e.g., May 1, 2026).
4) Change the Stage to an open stage (e.g., "Qualification" or "Negotiation"). 
5) Click Save
6) Go to Reports and run a report including this deal.
>Actual Behaviour:The deal moves back to the pipeline, but the Closing Date remains the original date (May 1, 2026). 
> Expected Behaviour:Ideally, when a deal is reopened, the Closing Date should be updated to a future date to accurately reflect the new sales forecast, or a custom field should be used to track the original close date.

4.isssue:Are automation logs accessible to a standard user, or only admins?
>Steps to Reproduce (Viewing Audit Logs)
1.Log into your Zoho CRM account.
2.Click the Settings (gear icon) in the top right corner.
3.Go to the Security Control section.
4.Click on Audit Log.
>Actual BehaviorAs an Admin: The user sees a comprehensive list of all actions, including "Workflow," "Webhooks," or "Functions," performed by any user in the organization.As a Standard User: The user sees a filtered list showing only their own actions and those of their subordinates, with no visibility into organization-wide or other teams' automation triggers.
>Expected BehaviorThe system should restrict viewing capabilities based on the profile permission. Only profiles with "Administrator" privileges should be able to see the full audit trail of all automations, while standard users' access is filtered.
